<title>POLAND: Polish broad money rises 3.1 pct in Dec 1-20 - NBP.</title>
<headline>Polish broad money rises 3.1 pct in Dec 1-20 - NBP.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-01-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland's broad money rose by 3.90 billion zlotys, or 3.1 percent, in December 1-20 to 131.78 billion after a 1.4 percent rise in November, preliminary central bank figures showed.  </p>
<p> BROAD POLISH MONEY		  DEC 1-20     NOV	DEC '95</p>
<p>  month/month change (pct)	    3.1	 1.4	   4.5</p>
<p>  Money in bln zlotys		 131.78    127.88	104.19</p>
<p>  Foreign currency (in bln PLN)    23.30     22.88	 21.30</p>
<p>  National currency		   108.48    105.00	 82.90</p>
<p>  Cash in circulation		  25.08     23.72	 19.53</p>
<p>  Lending to non-financial sector  79.94     76.94	 55.99</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
